url": "http://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio", "indices": [1167, 1190], "url": "https://t.co/z0WxBpwlXN"}, {"display_url": "github.com/zylon-ai/priva…", "expanded_url": "http://github.com/zylon-ai/private-gpt", "indices": [1254, 1277], "url": "https://t.co/jQeb6RcggL"}, {"display_url": "github.com/mem0ai/mem0", "expanded_url": "http://github.com/mem0ai/mem0", "indices": [1305, 1328], "url": "https://t.co/2AzDvOZElw"}, {"display_url": "github.com/AgentOps-AI/ag…", "expanded_url": "http://github.com/AgentOps-AI/agentops", "indices": [1362, 1385], "url": "https://t.co/seBG6fCh5C"}, {"display_url": "github.com/THUDM/AgentBen…", "expanded_url": "http://github.com/THUDM/AgentBench", "indices": [1420, 1443], "url": "https://t.co/BfSngb42sG"}, {"display_url": "github.com/elevenlabs/ele…", "expanded_url": "http://github.com/elevenlabs/elevenlabs-python", "indices": [1496, 1519], "url": "https://t.co/v1ZqYu3PEE"}, {"display_url": "github.com/deepgram/deepg…", "expanded_url": "http://github.com/deepgram/deepgram-python-sdk", "indices": [1523, 1546], "url": "https://t.co/DsGanIwElC"}], "user_mentions": []}, "id": "Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIxMDMwOTUxMDA4ODAzNTk0MjQ=", "text": "this is ultimate f*cking treasure.\n\n20 open-source projects that basically give you the entire AI agent stack for free.\n\nnot just another “top AI tools” list.\n\ntogether they cover the whole agentic loop:\n\nBUILD\n\n01 Ollama - run models locally ▸  ⁠https://t.co/bbPvy1btKB\n02 LangChain - wire LLM workflows ▸  ⁠https://t.co/w2AdRxxPGg\n03 Open Interpreter - let AI use your computer ▸  ⁠https://t.co/m42rPX3UMB\n04 AutoGen - build multi-agent systems ▸  ⁠https://t.co/5leQUbSdBE\n05 Aider - code with AI ▸  ⁠https://t.co/UjLV3aq4YZ\n\nORCHESTRATE\n\n06 AutoGPT - autonomous workflows ▸  ⁠https://t.co/mK2fbGHB6Q\n07 MetaGPT - software teams made of agents ▸  ⁠https://t.co/FEvhxdjPjN\n08 CrewAI - coordinate specialized agents ▸  ⁠https://t.co/tVukPP8BMm\n09 DSPy - optimize LLM pipelines ▸  ⁠https://t.co/yTxej7HI5Z\n10 CAMEL - multi-agent collaboration ▸  ⁠https://t.co/15vpxKBpjy\n\nACT\n\n11 Flowise - visual agent workflows ▸  ⁠https://t.co/yHqz6eKPoP\n12 Continue - AI inside your IDE ▸  ⁠https://t.co/nPVsDDOJiE\n13 Vercel AI SDK - ship AI apps ▸  ⁠https://t.co/ngeqtPP3jE\n14 E2B - give agents a sandbox ▸  ⁠https://t.co/peIqKgWyKg\n15 Composio - connect agents to real tools ▸  ⁠https://t.co/z0WxBpwlXN\n\nREMEMBER · TEST · SHIP\n\n16 PrivateGPT - private knowledge ▸  ⁠https://t.co/jQeb6RcggL\n17 Mem0 - agent memory ▸  ⁠https://t.co/2AzDvOZElw\n18 AgentOps - monitor agents ▸  ⁠https://t.co/seBG6fCh5C\n19 AgentBench - evaluate them ▸  ⁠https://t.co/BfSngb42sG\n20 ElevenLabs + Deepgram - voice in + voice out ▸  ⁠https://t.co/v1ZqYu3PEE▸  ⁠https://t.co/DsGanIwElC\n\nthe interesting part isn’t any single repo.\n\nit’s what happens when you connect them:\n\nmodel -> agent -> crew -> tools -> sandbox -> memory -> eval -> product\n\nyou don’t need to build an AI employee from zero anymore.\n\nthe pieces are already open source. you just have to assemble them.\n\nsave this before you build your next agent."}}}, "quoted_status_result": {"result": {"__typename": "Tweet", "article": {"article_results": {"result": {"cover_media": {"id": "QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHN/ihi3WQAAKAAIAAAAASGiJmQAA", "media_id": "2080630618790969344", "media_info": {"__typename": "ApiImage", "color_info": {"palette": [{"percentage": 93.6, "rgb": {"blue": 36, "green": 38, "red": 38}}, {"percentage": 2.88, "rgb": {"blue": 192, "green": 192, "red": 192}}, {"percentage": 0.78, "rgb": {"blue": 90, "green": 95, "red": 97}}]}, "original_img_height": 793, "original_img_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HN_ihi3WQAAHKCC.jpg", "original_img_width": 1983}, "media_key": "3_2080630618790969344"}, "id": "QXJ0aWNsZUVudGl0eToyMDgwNjMwNTM2NDE0OTIwNzA0", "lifecycle_state": {"modified_at_secs": 1784896923}, "metadata": {"first_published_at_secs": 1784896923}, "preview_text": "The free GitHub list that maps the entire AI agent ecosystem - 3